The <ansi fg="command">mudmail</ansi> command sends a mass in-game mail message to all players
(both online and offline). It is useful for announcements, patch notes,
or lore dispatches.

Usage: <ansi fg="command">mudmail</ansi> (launches an interactive prompt)

The prompt will ask for:
  <ansi fg="yellow">From name</ansi>  - The sender name displayed in the player's inbox (can be fictional)
  <ansi fg="yellow">Message</ansi>    - The body of the message
  <ansi fg="yellow">Gold</ansi>       - Optional gold amount to attach (0 for none)
  <ansi fg="yellow">Item</ansi>       - Optional item from your backpack to attach (or "none")
  <ansi fg="yellow">Confirm</ansi>    - Preview and confirm before sending

The mail is delivered to every player's inbox immediately and is also
queued for players who log in later.
